📐 The Ultimate Calibration Guide – WRO 2026 Future Engineers
This guide covers every tuneable parameter in your codebase – both in YAML and hardcoded values – with clear instructions on when, how, and why to calibrate each one.

🧭 Overview – Calibration Categories
Category	Where	Parameters	Priority
Physical Measurements	YAML (vehicle)	Wheelbase, max speed, max steering angle	🔴 High
Speed Control	YAML (navigation)	Base speed, boost, corner slowdown, predictive gain	🔴 High
Wall‑Following	YAML (navigation)	Wall‑follow gain, PID gains	🔴 High
Corner Detection	YAML (navigation.corner_detection)	Derivative threshold, percentage threshold, toggles	🟡 Medium
Traffic Lights	YAML (navigation.obstacle_challenge.traffic_light)	Distance start, min factor, LIDAR confirm range	🟡 Medium
Emergency Shield	YAML (ultrasonic_emergency_shield)	Stop/side/critical/hard shield thresholds, toggles	🔴 High
Parking	YAML (parking.emergency_shield)	Parking‑specific thresholds, toggles	🟡 Medium
Lap Counting	YAML (lap_counting)	Lap length, timeout, emergency margin	🔴 High
G‑Force Limiting	YAML (navigation.g_force)	Max safe G, filter alpha	🟡 Medium
Hardcoded (ESP32)	main.cpp	MAX_SPEED_MPS	🔴 High
Hardcoded (Python)	steering_controller.py, emergency_shield.py	Reverse speed, reverse duration, rear clearance threshold	🟡 Medium
📂 Part 1: YAML Parameters – How to Calibrate
1. Vehicle Physical Parameters (vehicle)
Parameter	Default	What It Does	How to Calibrate
wheelbase_m	0.25	Distance between front and rear axles (m).	Measure with a ruler – centre of front axle to centre of rear axle.
max_speed_mps	1.5	Absolute speed limit (m/s).	Start at 1.5, increase gradually until unstable, then reduce by 0.1.
max_steer_rad	0.524	Maximum steering angle (radians).	Measure servo max angle (e.g., 30° = 0.524 rad).
2. Navigation Speed Parameters (navigation.open_challenge / obstacle_challenge)
Parameter	Default	What It Does	How to Calibrate
base_speed_mps	1.5 / 1.3	Cruising speed.	Test lap times – increase until cornering becomes unstable.
straight_boost_factor	1.20 / 1.10	Speed multiplier on straights.	Increase if car feels slow on straights; decrease if unstable.
corner_slowdown_max_reduction	0.3 / 0.4	Max speed reduction in corners (0.3 = 30% reduction at max steer).	Increase if car understeers; decrease if car is too slow in corners.
predictive_slowdown_gain	0.3 / 0.4	How aggressively the car slows based on error derivative.	Increase if car enters corners too fast; decrease if too slow.
3. Wall‑Following & PID (navigation.pid)
Parameter	Default	What It Does	How to Calibrate
wall_follow_gain	0.30 / 0.25	Proportional gain for centering.	If car oscillates → decrease. If car drifts to one side → increase.
kp	25.0	Proportional gain (PID).	Start with default; increase for faster response, decrease for stability.
ki	0.1	Integral gain (PID).	Increase to eliminate steady‑state error (if car consistently hugs one wall).
kd	8.0	Derivative gain (PID).	Increase to reduce oscillation; decrease if car is jerky.
4. Corner Detection (navigation.corner_detection)
Parameter	Default	What It Does	How to Calibrate
use_derivative	True	Enable derivative‑based detection.	Keep True unless you have false positives.
use_percentage	True	Enable 40% change detection.	Keep True – it adds robustness.
use_graded_steering	True	Enable partial → full steering.	Keep True for smooth cornering.
use_imu_confirmation	True	Enable IMU confirmation.	Keep True to prevent false positives.
lidar_derivative_threshold	0.3	Sensitivity of derivative detection.	Decrease (e.g., 0.2) if corners are missed; increase (e.g., 0.4) if false positives.
pct_threshold	0.4	40% change threshold.	Adjust if corner detection is too early/late.
imu_confirm_threshold_radps	0.3	IMU yaw rate threshold.	Decrease if corners are missed; increase if false positives.
5. Traffic Lights (navigation.obstacle_challenge.traffic_light)
Parameter	Default	What It Does	How to Calibrate
distance_slowdown_start_m	2.0	Distance at which slowdown begins.	Increase for earlier slowdown; decrease for later.
distance_slowdown_min_factor	0.4	Minimum speed factor at close range.	Increase if car is too slow near pillar; decrease if too fast.
steering_slowdown_max_reduction	0.4	Max speed reduction from steering intensity.	Increase if car turns too sharply; decrease if car is too slow.
lidar_confirm_range_m	2.5	LIDAR confirmation range.	Increase if LIDAR has longer range; decrease if unreliable.
6. Emergency Shield (ultrasonic_emergency_shield)
Parameter	Default	What It Does	How to Calibrate
front_stop	12.0	Distance to start slowing down (cm).	Increase if car brakes too late; decrease if too early.
front_left_safety / front_right_safety	18.0	Side avoidance trigger distance (cm).	Increase if car hits side walls; decrease if too sensitive.
critical_stop	8.0	Distance to reverse/hard steer (cm).	Increase if car gets too close; decrease if too sensitive.
hard_shield_cm	5.0	Last‑resort emergency distance (cm).	Keep as safety net – adjust only if false triggers occur.
enable_reverse	True	Enable reverse on critical stop.	Keep True for safety.
enable_hard_shield	True	Enable hard shield.	Keep True for safety.
enable_hard_steer	True	Enable hard steer + crawl.	Keep True for parking lot escape.
7. Parking (parking.emergency_shield)
Parameter	Default	What It Does	How to Calibrate
front_stop	8.0	Relaxed front stop during parking (cm).	Increase if parking is too tight; decrease if too sensitive.
critical_stop	4.0	Relaxed critical stop during parking (cm).	Allow closer approach – 4 cm is safe.
hard_shield_cm	3.0	Relaxed hard shield during parking (cm).	Keep as last‑resort safety.
disable_reverse	False	Disable reverse during parking.	Set True if reverse interferes with parking.
disable_hard_steer	False	Disable hard steer during parking.	Set True if hard steer interferes with parking.
8. Lap Counting (lap_counting)
Parameter	Default	What It Does	How to Calibrate
lap_length_m	12.0	Full lap distance (m).	Push car around track, measure distance, update.
section_fallback_timeout_s	3.0	Time before odometry fallback (s).	Decrease if corners are missed; increase if false positives.
emergency_lap_margin_m	0.2	Distance margin for emergency lap completion.	Keep as safety net – adjust if laps are force‑completed too often.
9. G‑Force Limiting (navigation.g_force)
Parameter	Default	What It Does	How to Calibrate
max_safe_g	0.30	Maximum lateral G before speed reduction.	Increase (0.35) if car is stable at high speed; decrease (0.25) if rolling over.
filter_alpha	0.3	Low‑pass filter coefficient.	Increase for faster response; decrease for smoother.
📂 Part 2: Hardcoded Parameters (Code-Level)
1. ESP32 Firmware (esp32_firmware/src/main.cpp)
Parameter	Default	What It Does	How to Calibrate
MAX_SPEED_MPS	1.5	Absolute speed limit (must match YAML).	Change this AND YAML max_speed_mps together. Re‑upload firmware.
ULTRASONIC_TIMEOUT	15000	Ultrasonic pulse timeout (µs).	Keep at 15000 (15 ms) – enough for ~2.5 m range.
2. src/steering_controller.py
Parameter	Default	What It Does	How to Calibrate
self.reverse_speed	-0.10	Speed during reverse (m/s).	Increase if reverse is too slow; decrease if too fast.
self.reverse_duration	1.0	Duration of reverse (s).	Increase if car doesn't reverse enough; decrease if too much.
self.rear_clearance_threshold	0.15	Rear clearance required before reversing (m).	Increase if car hits objects while reversing; decrease if too cautious.
3. src/state_machine.py (Constants)
Parameter	Default	What It Does	How to Calibrate
MIN_AREA	120	Minimum pixel area for traffic light detection.	Increase if too many false positives; decrease if pillars are missed.
MAX_AREA	18000	Maximum pixel area for traffic light detection.	Decrease if large objects are mistaken for pillars.
MIN_ASPECT	1.5	Minimum aspect ratio (height/width) for pillars.	Increase if square objects are detected; decrease if pillars are missed.
MAX_ASPECT	4.0	Maximum aspect ratio for pillars.	Increase if tall objects are missed; decrease if false positives.
ROI_Y_MIN	30	Y‑position minimum for detection.	Adjust based on camera mounting height.
ROI_Y_MAX	210	Y‑position maximum for detection.	Adjust based on camera mounting height.
🧪 Calibration Procedure – Step by Step
Step 1: Measure Physical Parameters (Off‑Track)
Parameter	How to Measure
wheelbase_m	Use a ruler – front axle centre to rear axle centre.
max_steer_rad	Turn servo to max, measure wheel angle, convert to radians.
lap_length_m	Push car around the track, measure distance with a tape measure.
Step 2: Test Standalone (No Track)
Test	What to Check
Ultrasonic sensors	Check distances in logs – ensure all 3 sensors are reading correctly.
IMU	Check imu_yaw_rate in logs – should be ~0 when stationary.
HuskyLens	Check color detections – RED/GREEN IDs match YAML.
Motor + Servo	Test set_speed(0.3, 0) – car moves forward. Test set_speed(0, 0.3) – servo turns.
Step 3: Test on Track – Open Challenge
Priority	Parameter	Initial Value	Tuning Method
1	base_speed_mps	1.5	Increase until unstable, then reduce by 0.1.
2	wall_follow_gain	0.30	If oscillates → decrease; if drifts → increase.
3	corner_slowdown_max_reduction	0.3	Increase if understeer; decrease if too slow.
4	straight_boost_factor	1.20	Increase if straight feels slow; decrease if unstable.
5	MAX_SAFE_G	0.30	Increase if cornering feels safe; decrease if rollover.
Step 4: Test on Track – Obstacle Challenge
Priority	Parameter	Initial Value	Tuning Method
1	distance_slowdown_start_m	2.0	Increase if car approaches pillars too fast; decrease if too slow.
2	distance_slowdown_min_factor	0.4	Increase if car is too slow near pillars; decrease if too fast.
3	lidar_confirm_range_m	2.5	Increase if LIDAR has longer range; decrease if unreliable.
4	parking.emergency_shield.thresholds_cm	Defaults	Test parking – adjust if car touches walls or stops too early.
5	surprise_rule.turnaround_speed	0.1	Increase if U‑turn is too slow; decrease if unstable.
Step 5: Test Surprise Rule
What to Test	How
Trigger lap	Set trigger_lap: 1 and run – check that U‑turn happens after Lap 1.
Color detection	Ensure the last traffic light colour triggers the correct direction.
U‑turn speed	Adjust turnaround_speed if the turn is too slow or jerky.
