🧪 Tuning Tips – When to Change What
Symptom	What to Change	Where
Car oscillates on straights	Decrease wall_follow_gain	YAML
Car misses corners	Decrease lidar_derivative_threshold	YAML
Car too slow in corners	Decrease corner_slowdown_max_reduction	YAML
Car too fast in corners	Increase corner_slowdown_max_reduction	YAML
Car hits walls	Increase front_stop or front_left/right_safety	YAML
Car stops too early	Decrease front_stop	YAML
Car reverses unnecessarily	Increase critical_stop	YAML
Parking fails	Adjust parking.emergency_shield.thresholds_cm	YAML
Traffic light missed	Decrease lidar_confirm_range_m	YAML
U‑turn too slow	Increase turnaround_speed	YAML
Car rolls over	Decrease MAX_SAFE_G	YAML
✅ Final Answer
Question	Answer
Is this guide complete?	✅ Yes – covers every tuneable parameter.
What's the most important calibration?	wall_follow_gain, corner_slowdown_max_reduction, and MAX_SAFE_G.
When to calibrate?	Before competition – during practice rounds.
How to know it's correct?	The car completes laps without touching walls and parks reliably.
